Z||000049||2xsess||11-28-2000||04:16 PM||||I only have this to say. One of the major car mags did a comparison between an 84 Fiero and an 84MR2, I used to have a video. The Mr2 did better in some areas but the Fiero came out as their overall winner. <P>I don't have a problem with MR2s I actually like alot of Toyotas vehicles, I had a 90 Celica GTS that was quick and handled awesome. <P>Oh and Bluepearlsoul if you really want to see a decent FIero in your town get with member 1FST2M6 and maybe he'll take you for a ride in his  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 11-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000050||PearlBlueSoul||11-28-2000||04:30 PM||||HMM...Might have to take you up on that offer.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>1987 Toyota MR2 N/A 5 speed<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.atlantamr2s.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.atlantamr2s.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/darionscard</A>  <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/darionscard/Thumb.jpg">       <BR><B>Notable mods:</B>  Sus tech springs and sway bars, Toyota strut tower brace, KYB strut inserts, HKS exhaust, NGK plugs/wires, Momo Racer wheels (14x6), Custom intake, Kenwood 12" speaker in front trunk, Jensen amp.||||reg||1
Z||000051||Black88GT||11-28-2000||04:46 PM||||Wow I just caught up to all of this MR2 stuff.<P>I went to check out that MR2 forum, man what a joke that is.  The one guy was like "yeah why is the radiator in the back" and then everyone was talking about engine fires.  Then some a$$hole Fiero owners go over there and make it even worse by opening their big mouths about stuff they don't even know about.  Like that one guy who said the engine fires started because of an oil leak in the valve cover gasket.  <P>I have had mixed experiences with MR2 owners, some good some bad.  I was on the IMOC list for a year also.  When the Fiero came up there were a lot of people who were talking about V8 swaps and stuff, in amazement.  More respect then I would have thought.  Of course when the "engine fire" thing came up I had to set them straight, but they weren't as bad as that Mr2 forum, I am not even going to attempt to talk to those people.  I even had guys on the IMOC list emailing me personally for more info. on the Fiero, which gave me a new found respect for MR2 owners. It seems with MR2 owners, I can break them down into 3 categories.  <P>1.  Writes the Fiero off, "my car is best" mentality, brings up engine fires whenever fiero comes up<BR>2.  More open minded then 1 but still thinks Mr2's are better and "most" Fiero's suck (nothing wrong with that I guess)<BR>3.  Interested in other mid-engined designs like the Fiero and willing to accept any other car enthusiasts' love for their car, willing to ask about something they don't know about instead of making stuff up.<P>I was even going to get one at one point but couldn't justify the price or the extreme hike in insurance.<P>To the PearlBlue guy, that is one of the better looking MK1's I have seen, but it still looks like a doorstop to me and it is slow no matter how big the intake.  No flaming, just my opinion.  I think the 2m4 looks like crap too with the shovel nose, but thats just my opinion too.  I like the MK2 but the ones around here were running 9 grand (firm) and my insurance would have tripled (not exaggerating).   I think MR2 owners have an advantage since their cars were made longer, thus more improvements.  It's easy to make any stock fiero appear like junk when comparing it to a 95 turbo MK2 and all of its advanced features.  <P>To the MR2 fan, Fiero's were recalled all years, yes, but NOT for engine fires.  Cars are recalled all the time for little things.  I found it hillarious on that goofy MR2 forum that it affected over 600,000 cars, when there were about 300,000 Fiero's made.  Hmm...<P>I also found it amusing that there is a Lotus myth with MR2s also.  Seems we have more in common then we think. :-)<P>So basically people love their cars and others opinions do not matter, so why bother flaming each other over it?  I found a site where a guy dropped in a turbo engine from a Daytona into a K-CAR, he likes it so who are we to flame?<P>About the 6 grand Mk2 turbo, the only one I could find that cheap was one that had body damage.  I looked at 5 different Mk2 turbo's in 4 months and they all needed a turbo rebuild and other odds and ends, yet the owners wouldn't budge at $9,000.  The cheapest was $8,000 but it needed about $2,000 in work to pass inspection.  About those 500 Hp turbo's, what boost do they run?  How long will it last?  What octane gas do they have to use?  <P>The MK2 non turbo's are more like Del sols to me then "supercars" you proclaim them to be.  I was even thinking about buying an Mk2 N/A and swapping in a turbo motor, but everyone on the IMOC list said its cheaper/easier to just buy a turbo MR2.  What upgrades are avail. for the N/A Mk2 to get 400 Hp? 300 Hp? I sure couldn't find any.<P>I have more to say but I have to go to work so I will post later.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000052||1FST2M6||11-28-2000||04:48 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstlow_3.jpg"> <P>like this one! I've spoken to Bluepearl- before. I owned a Gold Fiero with Nitrous that was VERY closly watched on the local street racing scene here... I along with a fellow AE86 owner used to run alot around wreaking havoc. if your looking for a 4AGZE I have one. with 47K miles on it. T-Vis is a cool idea... and easy to manipulate. I'll be at Starbucks Town Center Tonite... 10pm.  <P>and whats with all these people thinking our cars catch on fire?!!? EXPLORERS DO TO!! faulty ign switchs! the pinto did when it got taged... the opel GT tail lights did for no reason.. EVERYTHING english with a positive ground would let the "magic smoke" out on occasion! GOOD GRIEF!!! <P><BR>AND YES!!! IT'S FASTER THAN YOUR FRIENDS CIVIC!!!!   <P><BR>sorry...  i've heard that at least once a day for the past 3 weeks... "well my friends civic will.." me- "no you know what your friends civic will do?!?! it's BUST the spider gears when he hits the nitrous button in a corner... THATS what your BUDDIES civic will do.."<P><BR>but i'm not annoyed..    sorry i'm usually not on edge.. just GOOD GRIEF! <P>------------------<BR>WOW... i've made chicken salad!!!||||reg||1
